      "notes": [
        "Dedicated native primitive: the surface decorator .awcRipple(…) / Modifier.awcRipple(…) (the composition md-ripple forms with its positioned parent) and the md-ripple node, with disabled, the six hooks (colour, opacity, both extents, grow duration and CSS easing text with the source's fallbacks) and the global --md-sys-ripple-enabled token.",
        "Methods through AWCRippleController: trigger() starts a centred, self-releasing wave; whenSettled() keeps the source's 200 ms bound and never settles a later wave.",
        "Only a primary press inside the rounded host shape starts a wave; the host's own gestures keep working. The origin is physical in RTL; a new press replaces the wave; disabling, losing the window/scene and leaving the hierarchy remove it.",
        "macOS SwiftUI, the iOS simulator and the Android emulator are verified against the Chrome oracles (paint, motion and behaviour); the ripple is hidden from assistive technologies."
